# 16. AUTOMATIONS AND BUSINESS RULES

Implement the following system automations:

1. A confirmed sale automatically deducts recipe ingredients.
2. A canceled sale reverses its inventory consumption.
3. A purchase increases ingredient stock.
4. A waste record decreases ingredient stock.
5. An adjustment corrects inventory stock.
6. A recipe modification updates future recipe costs.
7. Historical sales preserve their original costs.
8. Low-stock alerts appear when stock reaches or falls below minimum stock.
9. Dashboard KPIs update after relevant transactions.
10. Profitability reports update after sales and cost changes.
11. All important changes are recorded in an audit history.
12. Prevent duplicate transaction processing.

Transactions must be handled safely: if a sale cannot complete its required inventory movements, do not leave the sale and stock in inconsistent states.

